      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "One Last Thing",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "intro-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This is the last one. Demos are done, the code (mostly) works, and soon you'll scatter to jobs, grad school, and summer. But before you go, let's write this up in a way that is useful to you.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "intro-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "For years, I had teams write a Medium post. It was fine. The trouble is that ",
          "styles": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"we built an app\"",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " isn't necessarily something others are interested in reading. A case study, however, is much more useful to you as something you can show even if your project hosting goes away.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "7a230dcc-8f03-4207-ae5a-d013c82c796f",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "goal-callout",
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "textAlignment": "left",
        "emoji": "🎯"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Goal: ",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "As a team, you write one short debrief of the term and cut a video trailer everyone can reuse. Then each of you writes your own case study — the story of your role, your process, the evidence, and what you learned.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "spacer-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "h2-what-is",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "blue",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left",
        "level": 2,
        "isToggleable": false
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "What's a Case Study?",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "whatis-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A case study is the story of how you think, not just what you built: the problem you found, the approach you chose, what the data said, and what you'd do next. Designers and PMs have lived on these for years — engineers need them now too.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "whatis-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A blog post is a victory lap. A case study is ",
          "styles": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "evidence.",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " The difference is showing the messy middle — the pivot, the thing that broke, the metric you missed — and what you did about it. That's what makes someone believe you can do it again.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "whatis-example",
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "textAlignment": "left",
        "emoji": "📌"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Weak: ",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"We built a study-group finder with React and Firebase.\"   ",
          "styles": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Strong: ",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"Students in big intro courses told us they felt invisible, so we tested whether a 30-second group-matcher would actually get used.  80% surveyed said they would use it — but barely any came back after signup. Here's what that taught us about the real problem.\"",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "spacer-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "h2-trailer",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "blue",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left",
        "level": 2,
        "isToggleable": false
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The Team Trailer",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "trailer-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "🚀 As a team, cut ",
          "styles": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "one",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " short video trailer of your product. One trailer, shared — every teammate reuses it in their own case study, portfolio, and LinkedIn.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "trailer-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Keep it to 30–90 seconds. Show the product actually doing its thing, with a little polish and some advertising copy. You don't need to walk through every feature — future classes don't care that you have a login page, they want to feel what your product is about.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "trailer-why",
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "textAlignment": "left",
        "emoji": "💡"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This one lives on for posterity to inspire next year's teams — the same way the demos before you inspired you. Make it something you'd want your name on.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
